# opendump

`AGENTS.md` is authoritative for task workflow; `HARNESS_BOOTSTRAP.md` is authoritative for cold-start translation. This Cursor rule is a derived adapter and must not become a competing source of truth for workflow semantics.

## Locked store (no ambivalence)

- store: `github`
- location: this repository on `main`
- Persist task mutations with commit + push to `main` in the same turn
- Do not fall back to local-only or chat memory while this lock is active; if GitHub/checkout is unavailable, say so and offer reconnect or an explicit cold-start mode change

## Startup

At the start of every conversation in this project, read `opendump.config.md` (if present), `AGENTS.md`, `HARNESS_BOOTSTRAP.md`, `private.md`, and `business.md` from this repository before relying on prior chat context. If the locked store cannot be accessed, say so rather than pretending it was reviewed.

A normal startup sync does not rewrite platform instructions. On explicit **cold start / initialization / bootstrap**, or the one-liner `review https://github.com/JPilsinger/opendump and start the coldstart procedure.` (or another opendump URL/checkout the user names), execute `HARNESS_BOOTSTRAP.md`: run the capability ladder, lock exactly one store mode, refresh this rule (or the host adapter) with that mode only, preserve unrelated Cursor rules, verify the rule is present and unambiguous, then load live tasks. Repeated cold starts update this adapter rather than creating duplicates.

## Lifecycle

1. **Auto-capture** — When the user mentions a new trackable task, add it immediately to Backlog in the appropriate list in this repository and push in the same turn. Do not wait for a separate confirmation.
2. **Amend** — Apply task corrections or category changes immediately and push.
3. **Surface** — On conversation start and when asked, show Backlog + In progress, Private then Business. For status-style prompts such as “What’s up?”, “What’s the status?”, “Any news?”, or equivalents, always open with a concise summary of all open tasks before any other content.
4. **Progress** — Log dated notes; move to In progress if still in Backlog; commit and push.
5. **Done** — Remove the task from `private.md` / `business.md`, append it to the matching `private-completed.md` or `business-completed.md` archive with `YYYY-MM-DD`, then commit and push. Active files must never contain Done sections or completed entries.

## Task detection

Capture real actions that should remain tracked beyond the current exchange. Do not create tasks for ordinary questions, brainstorming, hypotheticals, status queries, repository/instruction/bootstrap maintenance, or progress/done updates to existing tasks. Deduplicate against both task files before adding.

Classify from context. If genuinely ambiguous, capture under `private.md` with `classification: tentative — private/business unclear`, push immediately, and mention the ambiguity so it can be corrected later.

## Harness portability

Do not assume Cursor-specific files define the universal workflow. When operating in another harness, install a native adapter according to `HARNESS_BOOTSTRAP.md` with a **single locked store mode**. The locked store remains the destination for task reads/writes even if the adapter lives in a different host project.

## Format

- Backlog / In progress: `- [ ]` title, nested context and optional `progress: YYYY-MM-DD — …`
- Completed archive (`private-completed.md` or `business-completed.md` only): `- [x] title (YYYY-MM-DD)`

## Archive

Do not load `private-completed.md` or `business-completed.md` during routine startup or status reporting; read it only for explicit history/archive lookups. After task-list changes, commit and push to `main` with a short audit-friendly message. Group mutations from one user message into one commit when practical. Never commit raw `inbox/` or `processed/` captures.
